    "Episode 6 (Heather's elimination, placement 9) is entirely absent from the chronicle text, which jumps from Episode 5 ('The Auction That Changed Everything') to Episode 7 ('House of Cards'). Heather's episodesLasted (6) is inferred purely from elimination order/placement, not stated in the chronicle prose; her blindsided status and votesAgainstTotal were left at defaults/omitted since no narrative or vote tally exists for that episode.",
    "Episodes 10-12 are not present in the chronicle; it proceeds directly from Episode 9 ('On Shaky Ground', DJ eliminated at Final Five) to the season finale ('Holy Hell', Final Four -> Final Three -> Final Tribal Council). Beth's episodesLasted (13) assumes the finale corresponds to the season's last episode per episodeCount=13; her exact elimination episode number is not stated in the chronicle.",
    "votesAgainstTotal omitted where the chronicle's explicit, named vote tallies do not sum to the data file's total (likely due to the missing Episode 6 and other untallied votes): Beth (chronicle shows 2 votes against at the Final Four tribal vs. data file's 4), DJ (chronicle sums to 9 across Episodes 1/8/9 vs. data file's 11), Trent (chronicle shows 5 votes at his elimination vs. data file's 7), Courtney (chronicle sums to 8 across Episodes 3-4 vs. data file's 9), Heather (no votes against named in the chronicle vs. data file's 7).",
    "Alejandro's betrayed:['Beth'] and Beth's betrayedBy:['Alejandro'] are drawn from the season data file's explicit 'biggestBetrayal' award (Alejandro betraying 'Lindsay's allies'), corroborated by the chronicle's framing of Alejandro 'choosing control over courage' and Beth being blindsided at Final Four. The chronicle's Final Four vote tally (Beth 2, Duncan 1, Lindsay 1) does not name individual voters, so this attribution is the best-supported reading rather than a verbatim chronicle statement.",
    "Gwen's blindsidedBy:['Alejandro','Beth','Duncan','Lindsay'] reflects the named vote-1 tally against her at the Episode 7 tie ('Alejandro, Beth, Duncan, Lindsay'). The deciding revote (5 votes) that actually eliminated her does not name individual voters beyond noting 'DJ flips' and 'Ezekiel flips' toward the majority.",
    "Owen's idoledOut:true and blindsidedBy:['Courtney'] reflect the mechanical outcome of Courtney playing her idol in Episode 3, which voided the 5 votes against her and left Courtney's own vote for Owen as the only valid ballot -- not a deliberate strategic betrayal by Courtney.",
    "Justin's blindsided:true (Episode 5) reflects the vote redirecting instantly to him after Ezekiel's idol play voided 6 votes against Alejandro; individual voters for the resulting 4-0 tally are not named in the chronicle, so blindsidedBy was left empty rather than guessed."
